@startuml
!include style.puml
hide empty description
title Example evolution of bounded destructive undo history

state "Live records: C; history (oldest to newest): A, B" as BeforeChange
state "Live records: D; history (oldest to newest): A, B, C" as AfterChange
state "Live records: E; history (oldest to newest): A, B, C" as AfterNewChange

BeforeChange --> AfterChange : normal change succeeds /\nsave D; append C; publish D
AfterChange --> BeforeChange : undo /\nsave C; publish C; remove C
BeforeChange --> AfterNewChange : normal change succeeds /\nsave E; append C; publish E

note bottom of AfterChange
The newest snapshot is restored first.
At the 100-snapshot limit, discard the oldest snapshot
before appending a new predecessor.
end note

note bottom of BeforeChange
No forward state D is retained.
end note
@enduml
